    "label": {},
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$impr_band5"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$impr_band5 is the 'villa threshold' — the top WOZ property-value cut-off in the tin_nl/BenCalc imputed-rent (amriv) calculation, above which a different formula (a fixed amount plus a marginal rate, $impr_perc_6, on the excess) applies instead of a flat percentage. Unlike the lower bands, this threshold is uprated annually: the Country Report's Table 2.27 shows it rising from €1,130,000 (2022) to €1,200,000 (2023), €1,310,000 (2024) and €1,330,000 (2025), and the constant's latest modelled value (€1,350,000) continues this trend into a later system year, consistent with its much higher number of recorded historical changes (10) versus the static lower bands."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: imputed rent (eigenwoningforfait), not in CR"
    },
